    "description": {
      "value": "\n<p><em>“Some stone was born yelling.”</em></p><p><strong>Menhirkin (Igneous).</strong> You are new rock. The Shattering was your birthday. The land that stood up and began answering chose you because it wanted a mouth that remembered being molten. You run hot, you cool slow, and you are, structurally, still furious about something.</p><h3>Traits</h3><ul><li><strong>Creature Type.</strong> Humanoid (Menhirkin).</li><li><strong>Size.</strong> Medium.</li><li><strong>Movement.</strong> 6 squares walking.</li><li><strong>Lineage Lean.</strong> Menhirkin does not grant fixed attribute bonuses; your background handles increases. Your heritage leans toward <strong>Violence</strong> in fiction and through Tier powers.</li></ul><h3>Menhirkin Core: The Land Stood Up</h3><p><em>Shared across all Menhirkin heritages. Granted at character creation via the base ancestry item.</em></p><ul><li><strong>Stone Soul.</strong> You count as Large for carry, shove, and grapple despite your Medium frame. You reroll the lowest die on checks to resist being forcibly moved.</li><li><strong>Hex Recognition.</strong> Once per scene, while you are on a natural surface you are directly touching, you may whisper a single question about the place. The GM answers with one true thing the land knows.</li><li><strong>Slow to Wear.</strong> You reroll the lowest die on Body checks against Stress, long-duration physical wear, forced marches, climate exposure, and sustained labor. You do not tire the way softer things tire.</li><li><strong>Heavy Presence.</strong> Your weight and settledness are perceptible. Creatures within 2 squares of you know you are there even if they cannot see you; you roll 3d10 keep lowest 2 on Intrigue (Stealth) checks unless you are on or in stone.</li></ul><h3>Igneous Traits</h3><ul><li><strong>Heat Memory.</strong> When you take thermal damage with the fire flavor, you may bank that damage. Before your next Soma Break, you may spend the banked heat as a bonus action to add +1d10 exploding thermal damage (flavor: fire) to your next weapon attack, unarmed strike, or grapple that connects.</li><li><strong>Molten Bearing.</strong> You count fire, smoke, ash, and heated terrain as normal ground for the purposes of difficult terrain and footing. Contact with your bare skin singes paper and warms metal.</li></ul><h3>Domain Edge</h3><ul><li><strong>Domain Edge.</strong> Your Domain gains <strong>+20 Violence marks</strong> and <strong>+20 Non-Lethal marks</strong> at campaign start.</li></ul><div data-ft-per-use=\"1\" style=\"margin-top:0.7rem;padding:0.55rem 0.75rem;border:1px solid #6a8caa;border-radius:0.35rem;background:rgba(55,75,95,0.18);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.78rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#a8c4e0;margin-bottom:0.25rem\">⟁ Per-Use Ability — <strong>Hex Recognition</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.86rem;opacity:0.92;line-height:1.4\"><strong>Recovery:</strong> 1/scene &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Action:</strong> Action &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Use:</strong> Click this feature on your sheet to invoke.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.82rem;opacity:0.85;margin-top:0.3rem\">On a natural surface you're touching, whisper a question — GM answers with one true thing the land knows.</div>\n</div>",
      "chat": ""
    },
